obligee of the antecedent duty. § 93. Promises Enumerated in §§ 82–85 Made in Ignorance of Facts A promise within the terms of §§ 82–85 is not binding unless the promisor knew or had reason to know the essential facts of the previous transac- tion to which the promise relates, but his knowledge of the legal effect of the facts is immaterial. § 94. Stipulations A promise or agreement with reference to a pending judicial proceeding, made by a party to the proceeding or his attorney, is binding without consideration. By statute or rule of court such an agreement is generally binding only § 90 RESTATEMENT OF CONTRACTS—SECOND"